<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Covadonga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 722</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Covadonga was fought in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a>, traditionally in 718 but more probably in 722, between a Muslim force and Asturian rebels led by the Visigothic noble Pelagius. Pelagius's victory, magnified in later chronicles, secured the independence of a small Christian realm that became the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturia">Asturias</a>, and Spanish tradition came to treat it as the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-covadonga.jpg" alt="Battle of Covadonga" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NACLE · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Invasionisl%C3%A1micaespa%C3%B1a.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
